== 4. Non-primitive integral points that the primitive test rejects (scope of the reduction)
  V2 point z=[1, 1, 2, 1, 1]: walls [2, 2, 2], gcd 2; normalized walls [1, 1, 1], marks at 1/2 and 5/2 (non-lattice)
  => a dark flat of this type is invisible to the primitive test but is covered by the unrestricted-integral Cramer bound of parametric-orbits.md with the same H.
